  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1035 AM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nRain/storm chances... CAMs are still showing a signal for\ndiurnal showers/storms percolating over the north this afternoon \ninto this evening where modest instability (1,000 to 1,500 J/kg)  \nbuilds. Agitated cu has already begun popping as of early this \nafternoon, though remain unsure whether or not elevated smoke will\nhinder further shower development. Regardless, no strong or \nsevere storms are expected, with most areas especially south of \nHwy 29 remaining dry with ridging overhead.\n\nNext chances for more widespread rain/thunder arrive Friday\nmorning, continuing into Saturday. Remain pessimistic about \nexcessive rainfall potential given a more southerly solution \npresented by 12Z suite of model runs, with higher PWATs (1.75\"+)\nholed up closer to the surface low. Additionally, dry air from\ndeparting high pressure persists to around 10k ft through Friday \nafternoon, delaying top down saturation of the profile. NBM\ncontinues to show broadbrush 40 to 60% chances for receiving 0.5\"\nof QPF confined along/south of the Hwy 10 corridor, which doesn't\nlend confidence to a forecast of widespread soaking rainfall.\nConvective activity should remain minimal due to weak shear (< 20\nknots) and limited forcing. Overall, signs point toward a period\nof light to moderate stratiform rain Friday and Friday night. \n\nExpect light rain to persist through Saturday morning as the cold\nfront continues to sag south. Dry weather should then settle in\nthrough around the mid-week timeframe as high pressure and upper\nridging build.\n\nSmoke... Expect air quality readings in the moderate (yellow)\ncategory today into Friday as subsidence from high pressure brings\nan elevated smoke plume near the surface. Per upstream obs, little\nto no deterioration in visibility are expected. Overall air \nquality impacts are not expected to be as drastic as earlier in \nthe month.",
